    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Ornstein Uhlenbeck Spread Backtest\"\nauthor: \"Rohan Jayanti, Yat Wai Heung\"\nformat:\n  html:\n    theme: superhero\n    embed-resources: true\n    toc: true\n    number-sections: true\n    code-fold: true\n    fig-width: 8\n    fig-height: 4.5\n    toc-depth: 3\nexecute:\n  echo: true\n  warning: false\n  message: false\njupyter: python3\n---\n\n\n# Ornstein Uhlenbeck Spread Backtest \n\nIn order to show that the OU process can be applied to pairs trading we will first construct a synthetic spread and then move to real life data. For real pairs, we first investigate a linear spread, given two asset price series. We then fit the OU model to the observed spread.\n\n## Backtest on Synthetic Spread\n\nLet us generate an OU process and treat it as if it were an observed spread.\n\nTake $\\theta = 2, \\mu = 0, \\sigma = 1$.\n\n::: {#247cf890 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport ornstein_uhlenbeck.ou as ou\nimport numpy as np\nimport plotly.graph_objects as go\n\nparams = ou.OUParams(\n    theta = 2.0,\n    mu = 0.0,\n    sigma = 1.0\n)\n\nx0 = 0.0\ndt = 0.01\nn_steps = 1000\nn_paths = 1\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n\nt = ou.time_grid(dt, n_steps)\npath = ou.simulate_paths(x0, params, dt, n_steps, n_paths, rng)\n\ndef apply_theme(fig):\n    fig.update_layout(\n        template=\"plotly_dark\",\n        paper_bgcolor=\"#111A22\",\n        plot_bgcolor=\"#111A22\",\n        font=dict(size=16),\n        width=799,\n        height=500,\n        legend=dict(\n            orientation=\"h\",\n            yanchor=\"bottom\",\n            y=1.02,\n            xanchor=\"right\",\n            x=1,\n        ),\n    )\n    return fig\n\nfig = go.Figure()\nfig.add_trace(\n    go.Scatter(\n        x = t,\n        y = path[:,0],\n        name = \"Simulated path\",\n        mode = \"lines\",\n    )\n)\n\nfig.add_hline(\n    y = params.mu,\n    line_dash = \"dash\",\n    annotation_text = \"Long-run mean\",\n)\n\nfig.update_layout(\n    title = \"Single Ornstein-Uhlenbeck sample path\",\n    xaxis_title = \"Time\",\n    yaxis_title = \"State\"\n)\n\napply_theme(fig)\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div>            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.5/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS-MML_SVG\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-3.4.0.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-KEmPoupLpFyGMyGAiOsiNDbKDKAvxXAn/W+oQa0ZAfk=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"8ee9c9e1-f8e0-4ec3-ab6c-d90adde26652\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:500px; width:799px;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"8ee9c9e1-f8e0-4ec3-ab6c-d90adde26652\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"8ee9c9e1-f8e0-4ec3-ab6c-d90adde26652\",                        [{\"mode\":\"lines\",\"name\":\"Simulated path\",\"x\":{\"dtype\":\"f8\",\"bdata\":\"AAAAAAAAAAB7FK5H4XqEP3sUrkfhepQ\\u002fuB6F61G4nj97FK5H4XqkP5qZmZmZmak\\u002fuB6F61G4rj\\u002fsUbgeheuxP3sUrkfherQ\\u002fCtejcD0Ktz+amZmZmZm5Pylcj8L1KLw\\u002fuB6F61G4vj+kcD0K16PAP+xRuB6F68E\\u002fMzMzMzMzwz97FK5H4XrEP8P1KFyPwsU\\u002fCtejcD0Kxz9SuB6F61HIP5qZmZmZmck\\u002f4XoUrkfhyj8pXI\\u002fC9SjMP3E9CtejcM0\\u002fuB6F61G4zj8AAAAAAADQP6RwPQrXo9A\\u002fSOF6FK5H0T\\u002fsUbgehevRP4\\u002fC9Shcj9I\\u002fMzMzMzMz0z\\u002fXo3A9CtfTP3sUrkfhetQ\\u002fH4XrUbge1T\\u002fD9Shcj8LVP2dmZmZmZtY\\u002fCtejcD0K1z+uR+F6FK7XP1K4HoXrUdg\\u002f9ihcj8L12D+amZmZmZnZPz4K16NwPdo\\u002f4XoUrkfh2j+F61G4HoXbPylcj8L1KNw\\u002fzczMzMzM3D9xPQrXo3DdPxWuR+F6FN4\\u002fuB6F61G43j9cj8L1KFzfPwAAAAAAAOA\\u002fUrgehetR4D+kcD0K16PgP\\u002fYoXI\\u002fC